+# Perf history
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+Change: took `PRAGMA quick_check` off the health-gate read path, and added the
+`fts_rows` counter check and the `body` CHECK constraint at the same time.
+
+Numbers available from a Muninn session-transcript record (trust 1 —
+`origin: tool_observed`, observed in this project's own session history, not
+independently confirmed by an exit code or a commit):
+
+- Before: **11.9 ms**
+- After: **1.05 ms**
+
+(evidence: `~/.local/share/muninn-bench/seed-14a6ab47-frozen.jsonl:22559233`)
+
+Caveat: this record only states the two SessionStart timings above. It does
+not say these are p50 (vs. a single run or some other statistic), and it does
+not say the store held 5k records at the time of measurement. `muninn why`
+against this question comes back `insufficient: only circumstantial records
+(trust < 2)` — no trust-2/3 record (confirmed by an exit code or a commit, or
+stated by the user) corroborates a p50-on-5k-records framing. So: the 11.9 ms
+→ 1.05 ms drop for this exact change (quick_check off the read path + fts_rows
+counter + body CHECK) is what's recorded, but a measured p50 specifically on a
+5k-record store could not be found here. Not inventing one.
